      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #1): ↑ of a disclosed, enlisted,
      ⍝ or each'ed lvalue as a selective-specification target segfaulted
      ⍝ (NULL owner in Value::assign_cellrefs()). It now assigns through
      ⍝ the selected cell, like the plain control V←1 2 3 ◊ (↑⊃V)←9.
      ⍝
      V←(1 2)(3 4) ◊ (↑⊃V)←9 ◊ V
 9 2  3 4 

      V←(1 2)(3 4) ◊ (↑∊V)←9 ◊ V
 9 2  3 4 

      V←(1 2)(3 4) ◊ (↑↑¨V)←9 ◊ V
 9 2  3 4 

      V←2 2⍴(1 2)(3 4)(5 6)(7 8) ◊ (↑⊃V)←9 ◊ V
 9 2  3 4 
 5 6  7 8 

      V←1 2 3 ◊ (↑⊃V)←9 ◊ V
9 2 3

      ⍝ ↑ selects one cell, so more values than that is a LENGTH ERROR
      ⍝
      V←(1 2)(3 4) ◊ (↑⊃V)←9 9
LENGTH ERROR+
      (↑⊃V)←9 9
      ^    ^

      )SIC
      V
 1 2  3 4 

      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #2): ∊ of a disclosed lvalue as
      ⍝ a selective-specification target segfaulted (the right-value
