      ⍝ regression (Bugs32 #10): a )COPY'd file that ended while ]FILE_CTL
      ⍝ skipping swallowed the rest of the calling file (this one)
      ⍝
      F10←'/tmp/ZZ71_Bugs32_10.apl'



      WRITE F10 ('#!./apl --script' 'Z1←1' ']FILE_CTL SKIP_ALL' 'Z2←2')



      )COPY /tmp/ZZ71_Bugs32_10.apl
DUMPED ³



      Z1 (⎕NC 'Z2')
1 0



      )ERASE Z1



      ⍝ the skip mode of the input source that )COPYs a file is restored at
      ⍝ the end of that file, at any depth of nested )COPYs: F (this file)
      ⍝ copies G, G copies H, and each file ends in a different skip mode.
      ⍝ After the )COPY, this file must continue normally, while HX and GX
      ⍝ (after SKIP_ALL in H and SKIP_GNU in G) must not be defined.
      ⍝ (]FILE_CTL without an argument shows the current skip mode, but
      ⍝ like all ] commands it writes to CERR, which is not compared here.)
      ⍝
      FG←'/tmp/ZZ71_Bugs32_G.apl' ◊ FH←'/tmp/ZZ71_Bugs32_H.apl'



      WRITE FH ('#!./apl --script' ']FILE_CTL SKIP_ALL' 'HX←1')



      WRITE FG ('#!./apl --script' ']FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2' (')COPY ',FH) 'G2←2' ']FILE_CTL SKIP_GNU' 'GX←1')



      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2



      )COPY /tmp/ZZ71_Bugs32_G.apl
DUMPED ³



      ]FILE_CTL NO_SKIP



      (⎕NC 'HX') (⎕NC 'GX') G2
0 0 2



      ⍝ only the exact mode words are accepted (Bugs32 #29): SKIP_GNUXX
      ⍝ used to be taken as SKIP_GNU, which skipped the next line
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_GNUXX



      ⎕←'not skipped'
not skipped



